═══ R8 EN reply complete (collagen/vegetarian) — guard: passed_after_retry ═══
Q: I have spondylosis and osteoporosis and my doctor requires me to take collagen as part of treatment. But I have been a vegetarian for 14 years. Can I take normal collagen?
Sources: Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) | Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: qa_metaphysics,qa_general,introduction,canonical_ruling
  ✓ substantial reply (>600 chars)
  ✓ ends cleanly (punctuation/emoji, not mid-word)
  ✓ answers the vegetarian-collagen question
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
This is a really thoughtful question, and it shows how seriously you take both your health and your vows 🙏

Master Lu addressed this kind of situation in the *Buddhism Q&A*. When it comes to medicine or health supplements containing animal by-products like gelatine or fish oil, he said:

> When you consume any medicine or health supplements that contain ingredients such as gelatine or fish oil, if your body does not reject the taste, then perhaps you have not reached the level where you are completely observing your precepts. However, it would still be best to avoid consuming such products as they contain animal by-products.

So Master Lu's guidance leans toward **trying your best to avoid** animal-derived supplements — but he also acknowledged the reality that sometimes it's not straightforward.

Here are some practical considerations based on his teachings:

**1. Look for plant-based collagen alternatives first**
There are now marine collagen substitutes and plant-based collagen boosters (from vitamin C, silica, and amino acid combinations) available. These would be the most ideal option to explore with your doctor.

**2. If animal collagen is medically necessary**
Master Lu taught us that taking care of our body is also important — Bodhisattvas want us to be healthy so we can continue practising. If your doctor says it is truly necessary and no plant-based alternative works, you can sincerely say to Guan Yin Bodhisattva in your heart that you are consuming it out of medical necessity and not by choice.

**3. Recite more to replenish**
You can recite the **Eighty-Eight Buddhas Great Repentance (《礼佛大忏悔文》)** sincerely to repent, and recite **《往生净土神咒》(往生咒)** to help the small spirits involved.

**4. Discuss with your doctor**
Ask your doctor specifically whether plant-based collagen support could achieve similar results for your spondylosis and osteoporosis — some doctors are open to this.

You've kept your vegetarian vow for 14 years — that itself is tremendous merit 🙏 Master Lu always taught us to do our best within our circumstances, with a sincere heart. Bodhisattva understands.

